jobs.description:
Front-End SW Engineer

## ABOUT DELVITECH

Delvitech stands at the forefront of technological advancement, having pioneered innovative Automatic Optical Inspection (AOI) technology for assembled printed circuit boards (PCB) utilizing artificial intelligence. Our accomplished team is driven by a commitment to exceed technological boundaries and consistently deliver exceptional results. We are actively seeking individuals who are eager to embrace challenges, contribute proactively to achieving our set objectives, and play a pivotal role in propelling the company’s growth. Presently, an opportunity exists for a proficient and motivated Front-End Software Engineer

## JOB DESCRIPTION

We are seeking a dedicated and highly skilled Front End SW Engineer / Front End Developer. The Front-End Engineer is responsible for developing and implementing the user interface of web applications and software. He/she works closely with UX/UI designers and back-end developers to create intuitive and high-performance user experiences. The role involves writing efficient code, optimizing performance, ensuring cross-browser compatibility, and managing user interactions. He is responsible for curating the structure of server side information. Back Side Engineers primarily write server scripts and API’s to be utilized by front side engineers and UX designers. The day to day consist of optimizing servers for speed and stability, implementing security structures, generating reusable code libraries and generating data storage solutions to join our team. This role is based at our headquarters in Mendrisio. The ideal candidate will bring a patient, organized, and problem-solving approach to their work and must have prior experience in a similar field.

## KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

- Design and develop modern, responsive user interfaces using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript;
- Implement UI components using frameworks such as React, Vue.js, or Angular;
- Collaborate with the UX/UI team to transform designs into functional interactive experiences;
- Optimize application performance to ensure smooth and fast navigation;
- Ensure cross-browser and cross-platform compatibility;
- Apply accessibility principles (WCAG) to guarantee inclusivity and usability;
- Integrate APIs and back-end services for data retrieval and management;
- Implement automated testing to ensure code stability and maintain quality;
- Contribute to the creation and maintenance of reusable UI component libraries;
- Collaborate with the development team to improve coding processes and best practices.

## REQUIREMENTS

- Master’s Degree or PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or equivalent experience;
- Experience in front-end development and building scalable user interfaces;
- In-depth knowledge of:
- HTML5, CSS3 (SASS/LESS), JavaScript (ES6+);
- Front-end frameworks/libraries (React, Vue.js, Angular)
- Responsive Design and CSS frameworks (Tailwind, Bootstrap, Material UI);
- State management (Redux, Vuex, Zustand, Recoil);
- Web performance optimization (Lazy Loading, Code Splitting, Caching);
- Testing and debugging (Jest, Cypress, React Testing Library);
- Version control: Git, GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket;
- CI/CD and DevOps for front-end (Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Actions).
- Open minded and ability to work in a multidisciplinary team;
- Problem solving skills and reasoning ability;
- Capacity for attention to detail;
- Self-motivated with a creative pioneer spirit;
- Interpersonal skills;
- Oral and written communicative capabilities;
- Must work well in teams with other Engineering disciplines, including Electrical, Electronical, Optical and Software.

If this position matches your skills and aspirations, please send your complete application, including CV and references, to career@delvi.tech with your name and “Front End SW Engineer / Front End Developer” in the subject line. Only short list candidates will be contacted.

## APPLY NOW

